      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Where would the stream camera stream to? On PC, your PC monitor just shows the stream camera view while still sending the first person perspective to the connected headset. This operation also presumably takes up alot of ram, something the quest platform struggles with. \n\nMaybe it could stream to a phone app? And maybe this app could offload some of the stress of the ram from the quest headset. But I don't know the logistics of programming that, if it's even possible. \n\nAnother option would be to stream to a streaming application on a computer, but that just defeats the purpose of not needing a PC. \n\nQuest streaming camera would be very cool, but the game struggles to run on quest 2 with the browser playing music in the background, how is it going to manage two different video streams? Ram is already so limited for the quest hardware.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
